## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/edgedetectcontour.html
- Summary (EN): Finds silhouette outlines and draws them with varying widths by comparing each pixel's input value, such as a primitive ID, with its neighbours using ray differentials.
- Résumé (FR) : Trace des contours de silhouette d'épaisseur variable en comparant chaque pixel à ses voisins.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: signal to run silhouette detection on", "thickness: optional input varying line thickness"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Thickness Scale: kernel radius in pixels; a multiplier when thickness is connected", "Edge Spread: spread of the Gaussian weight, controlling edge falloff", "Blur: blurs the image before detection", "Contour Tolerance: minimum difference from neighbours for a pixel to count as part of the line", "Min Probe Radius: minimum search radius for probe pixels"]

- Caveats: ["The page gives no default values, numeric ranges or interaction guidance; tuning needs experiments.", "Covers silhouettes only; crease lines are for Edge Detect by Normal and self-occluding depth edges for Edge Detect by Depth."]

